# App Router rules

Generated from AGENTS.md — do not hand-edit. Regenerate with `npx @codeandtheory/sdp generate-rules`.

## Server-first rendering
React Server Components by default. A Client Component (`"use client"`) is an explicit, justified exception. Do not add `"use client"` just to unblock a hook; push state up or restructure.

## App Router conventions
- Route segments live under `app/` only — no `pages/` directory.
- Route-specific UI uses Next.js file conventions: `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`.
- Shared UI lives under `app/ui/`. Library code (data, actions, types, utils) lives under `app/lib/`.

## Server Actions
Mutations go through Server Actions (`"use server"` in `app/lib/actions.ts`). Validate all inputs at the action boundary using Zod before any database write.

## Database access
Never query the database directly from a UI component or a page — use functions from `app/lib/data.ts` (reads) or `app/lib/actions.ts` (mutations) only.

## Spec gate
No code changes without a governing, approved spec. A story's Tier 2 spec is the first commit on its feature branch.
